GRWM to dive 200m under the Canadian Arctic in a real submarine!!!❄️🌊 

These state-of-the-art subs on @seabourncruise can reach depths of 300m (1,000 ft), taking you into places almost no one gets to see. 

On land it’s all ice and tundra, but under the sea? A whole other world filled starfish, anemones, jellyfish, even in -1.5°C water. We were a bit nervous at first (who wouldn’t be- especially because I don’t dive) but it was surprisingly calming once we began to descend. 

Truly one of the most surreal experiences of our travels- who knew we would be floating around in a submarine in Nunavut?!?

Would you take the plunge?👀

